      "content": "<h3>How a duplicate is detected</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>hash(e) -> bucket -> equals()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> true / false</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1) average</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> When you <code>add</code> an element, the backing map hashes it, goes to the bucket, and compares with every node there: first by <strong>hash</strong>, then by <code>==</code> or <code>equals</code>. A match means \"duplicate\": the map keeps the old key and <code>add</code> returns false.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Note: when a duplicate is rejected, the <strong>old object stays in the set</strong>; the new one is thrown away. This matters if the two objects are equal but not identical.</p>",
