      "content": "<h3>null in a HashSet and fail-fast iterators</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>add(null)  and  for-each + add()</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> allowed / ConcurrentModificationException</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> A HashSet allows <strong>one null</strong> element (HashMap allows a null key, stored in bucket 0). Its iterator is <strong>fail-fast</strong> through the map's <code>modCount</code>: adding or removing during a loop throws <code>ConcurrentModificationException</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Remove during iteration with <code>iterator.remove()</code> or <code>removeIf</code>.</p>",
