      "content": "<h3>The real source of java.util.HashSet (simplified)</h3>\n<p>The implementation is so small that its core fits in this list.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>public boolean add(E e) { return map.put(e, PRESENT) == null; }</code></li>\n<li><code>public boolean contains(Object o) { return map.containsKey(o); }</code></li>\n<li><code>public boolean remove(Object o) { return map.remove(o) == PRESENT; }</code></li>\n<li><code>public Iterator&lt;E&gt; iterator() { return map.keySet().iterator(); }</code></li>\n<li><code>public int size() { return map.size(); }</code></li>\n<li><code>clone()</code> copies the backing map; serialization writes the elements, capacity and load factor (the map field is <code>transient</code>).</li>\n<li>A package-private constructor <code>HashSet(int, float, boolean dummy)</code> creates a <code>LinkedHashMap</code>: that is how <code>LinkedHashSet</code> reuses all of HashSet.</li>\n</ul>"
