      "content": "<h3>Best practices</h3>\n<p>Everything about HashSet follows from the HashMap inside it.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Elements must implement <code>equals</code> and <code>hashCode</code> consistently (or be <code>record</code>s / strings / numbers / enums).</li>\n<li>Use immutable elements, or never change fields used by <code>hashCode</code> while the object is in a set.</li>\n<li>Presize a large set: <code>new HashSet&lt;&gt;((int) (n / 0.75f) + 1)</code> (or <code>HashSet.newHashSet(n)</code> in Java 19+).</li>\n<li>Do not rely on iteration order; choose LinkedHashSet or TreeSet if order matters.</li>\n<li>For thread safety use <code>ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet()</code> or <code>Collections.synchronizedSet</code>.</li>\n</ul>"
